Our algorithm is correct because of how we split up the array. Everything in the smaller sub array is less than the pivot, everything in equal is the pivot, and everything in greater is bigger than the pivot. So if the array was sorted smaller would come first then equal then greater. This means if K is less than or equal to the size of smaller the answer has to be in smaller. If K is in the range of the equal array then the answer is the pivot. If K is bigger than both then the answer is in greater, and we subtract the size of smaller and equal from K so it still points to the right number.

We also know it will always finish because the pivot is always taken out of the array before the next call, so the sub array always gets smaller. Eventually the sub array will be size 1 or K will be in the equal array and the pivot gets returned.